[b][size=150]Shatranj 1.0 "Opening Move"[/size][/b]
[b]Online chess for a real ZX Spectrum 48K[/b][/center]

Hello everyone.

This is the first official release of [b]Shatranj[/b]: an online chess application built for a [b]real ZX Spectrum 48K[/b], with Spectrum-to-Spectrum and Spectrum-to-PC play.

This is not just a modern app styled after the Spectrum. The Spectrum side owns the board, move entry, clocks, chat, move history, setup screens, session state, and network protocol inside the 48K target.

[b]Download[/b]

[url=https://github.com/IgnacioMonge/Shatranj/releases/tag/v1.0]Shatranj 1.0 - Opening Move[/url]

[list]
[*][b]SHATRANJ-1.0-spectrum.zip[/b] - Spectrum package. Includes [b]SHATRANJ.tap[/b], [b]SHATRANJ.OVL[/b], and [b]SHATRANJ.DAT[/b]. Keep the three files together.
[*][b]Shatranj-Client-Setup-1.0.exe[/b] - Windows installer for the PC client.
[*][url=https://github.com/IgnacioMonge/Shatranj]GitHub repository[/url]
[/list]

[b]Spectrum requirements[/b]

[list]
[*]Real ZX Spectrum 48K.
[*]divMMC/esxDOS.
[*]ESP-AT network link over UART.
[*]Direct TCP requires a reachable peer. If NAT/CGNAT gets in the way, MQTT is the intended route.
[/list]

[b]Game modes[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Spectrum-Spectrum[/b]: two network-connected Spectrums play each other.
[*][b]Spectrum-PC[/b]: one Spectrum plays against the bundled Qt desktop client.
[*][b]Direct TCP[/b]: for local networks or reachable forwarded ports.
[*][b]MQTT[/b]: broker-mediated play when direct connectivity is not practical.
[/list]

[b]What is included in 1.0[/b]

[list]
[*]Complete Spectrum board UI, coordinate move entry, and explicit Send Move confirmation.
[*]Clocks, move history, chat with side icon and timestamp.
[*]Chat length matched to the real visible two-line Spectrum envelope.
[*][b]Connection Setup[/b] and [b]Game Setup[/b] menus.
[*]Host/Guest, side/color policy, transport, endpoint, port, room code, notation, hints, theme, and piece-set setup.
[*][b]/draw[/b] and [b]/resign[/b] commands with confirmation flow.
[*]Reset/restart, disconnect, opponent-ready, check, checkmate, and rematch flows.
[*]Three 16x16 piece sets: [b]BRRY[/b], [b]SPCY[/b], and [b]PIXL[/b].
[*]Five board themes: Classic, Blue, Green, Cyan, and Magenta.
[*]Qt PC client with interactive board, chat, clocks, RX/TX log, and Direct/MQTT support.
[/list]

[b]Technical work included[/b]

[list]
[*]Spectrum build with z88dk + SDCC/IY.
[*]2 KB esxDOS/divMMC overlays for cold code paths.
[*]DAT package for runtime assets, pieces, and About-screen artwork.
[*]Readable protocol for game start, moves, ACK/NACK, chat, ping, reset, draw, resign, and BYE.
[*]Build guards for resident size, overlays, ABI, low-RAM layout, BSS, and stack margin.
[*]Stability work across Direct TCP, MQTT, UART, reconnect paths, remote move validation, and terminal states.
[*]Measured Z80 optimisation work on piece blitting, rendering, keyboard scan, text paths, rules/SAN helpers, and MQTT buffers.
[/list]

